  "term": "hyperglycemia",
  "definition": "Hyperglycemia is a state of high glucose concentration. In this source, it is described as something that can be triggered by tuberculosis infection, stress linked to the illness, or rifampicin-related metabolites, and may contribute to later type 2 diabetes in people who were not previously diabetic.",
